SUMMARY:Lang Pioneer Village - Applefest
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a fun-filled celebration of apples and the harvest season with\nApplefest at Lang Pioneer Village Museum! The Museum’s sweetest and most popular\nevent returns to the historic village on Sunday\, September 27\, from 10 am to 4 pm.\nTour the village by horse-drawn wagon courtesy of Highview Farm\, and enjoy the\nsights\, tastes\, and aromas of autumn and apples. View a wide variety of historic\ndemonstrations throughout the village\, including cider pressing at the Cider Barn\, threshing\, mattress repair and\nstuffing\, sheep shearing\, natural dyeing\, chair caning\, grinding at the Grist Mill\, woodturning by the Peterborough\nArtisan Centre Wood Turners and Kawartha Wood Turners Guild\, and more.\nView an antique clock display brought by the Quinte Timekeepers\, and see the many entries that were submitted for\nthe Peterborough Agricultural Society’s Homecraft Show in the Peterborough County Agricultural Heritage Building.\nEnjoy traditional music performed by Lotus White on the Weaver Shop porch\, play apple tic-tac-toe\, and participate in\nold-fashioned schoolyard games. Children\, enjoy story time and make a craft with the Otonabee South-Monaghan\nPublic Library.\nIf you are feeling hungry\, visit the Peterborough County Agricultural Heritage Building courtyard\, where the Bewdley\nLions Club food truck will be selling BBQ goods (cash only)\, and Call Creations Catering & Events will have a variety\nof food items available for purchase. Pick up some traditional fall fair fare from Ben’s Kettle Corn\, which will be selling\nkettle corn and candy floss. Enjoy apple cider and freshly baked apple treats at the Keene Hotel. There will be bushels\nof sweet\, juicy apples\, candy apples\, and fresh apple cider available for purchase to take home with you.\nTickets for the event are available for purchase in advance online and at the door. On-site parking is available on a\nfirst-come\, first-served basis. Overflow parking for the event is available at McIntyre Park.\nImmerse yourself in the colourful beauty of fall in the historic village and celebrate all things apple during Applefest\,\nSunday\, September 27\, from 10 am to 4 pm at Lang Pioneer Village Museum. Admission is $17 for adults\, $12 for\nstudents and seniors (60+)\, $9 for youths (ages 5-14)\, and free for children under 5. Family admission is also available\nfor $45 and includes 2 adults and up to 4 youths ages 5-14.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/lang-pioneer-village-applefest-2/
LOCATION:Lang Pioneer Village Museum\, 104 Lang Rd\, Keene\, ON\, K0L 2G0\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Lang Pioneer Village Museum":MAILTO:media@langpioneervillage.ca
